Subject: [PATCH] vip: skip fully transparent background character rows

DrawBG's aligned path tested each of a character row's eight 2-bit
pixels before writing it. Background layers often have empty areas,
where all eight are 0 (transparent) and nothing is written: test the row
once. Output is bit-identical.

diff --git a/mednafen/vb/vip_draw.inc b/mednafen/vb/vip_draw.inc
index 8024feb..685ef2c 100644
--- a/mednafen/vb/vip_draw.inc
+++ b/mednafen/vb/vip_draw.inc
@@ -70,7 +70,11 @@ static void DrawBG(uint8 *target, uint16 RealY, bool lr, uint8 bgmap_base_raw, b
   {
    uint32 pixels = CHR16[char_no * 8 + char_sub_y];
 
-   if(bgsc & 0x2000)
+   /* A fully transparent character row writes nothing (A12/A13: empty
+    * background areas are common and cost eight tests each). */
+   if(!pixels)
+    ;
+   else if(bgsc & 0x2000)
    {
     if((pixels >> 14) & 3) target[0 + x] = GPLT_Cache[palette_selector][(pixels >> 14) & 3];
     if((pixels >> 12) & 3) target[1 + x] = GPLT_Cache[palette_selector][(pixels >> 12) & 3];
